  "display_title": "Foster Care",
  "description": "Si-Wu doesn’t do relationships — just low-maintenance hookups with no strings attached. So when Hui-Won, a younger classmate with no apparent sex drive, a great body, and a frustratingly handsome face, starts hanging around, Si-Wu figures he’s found the perfect arrangement.\n\n *“Hyung, you’re more good-looking in my eyes... You're so handsome…”*\n\nBut Hui-Won barrels in without hesitation, and the emotional walls Si-Wu built so carefully don’t stand a chance. As Hui-Won keeps crossing lines and closing distance, Si-Wu keeps telling himself the same thing:\n\n*\"It'll be like taking care of a stray dog... I'll just offer him foster care until someone better comes along.\"*\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
